### Issue description

Minecraft 1.16.5 Forge 36.2.35 Crafttweaker 7.1.2.533

When player interact with blocks, RightClickBlockEvent always ignore the offhand of player.

```zenscript
crafttweaker.api.events.CTEventManager.register<crafttweaker.api.event.entity.player.interact.MCRightClickBlockEvent>(event => {
    if (event.player.world.getBlockState(event.blockPos).block == <block:minecraft:crafting_table> ) {
        if (event.player.world.remote) return;
        event.player.sendMessage(event.itemStack.commandString);
        event.player.sendMessage(event.hand as string);
    }
});

crafttweaker.api.events.CTEventManager.register<crafttweaker.api.event.entity.player.interact.MCEntityInteractEvent>(event => {
    if (event.target.type == <entitytype:minecraft:pig> ) {
        if (event.player.world.remote) return;
        event.player.sendMessage(event.itemStack.commandString);
        event.player.sendMessage(event.hand as string);
    }
});
